## Context

Layer of the three-scope authority model: this spec is normative for
`.dyne` files -- a hand-edited file that satisfies it is valid
regardless of binary version. Autonomous from `erg spec`: same
three-section grammar by imitation, not by citation (the shared
mini-spec is deferred per 0270). Blocked by the PEP (0271), which
arbitrates intent.

## Scope

Mirror the `%erg 0.1` spec's structure, for MRs:

- extension `.dyne`, location `tickets/merges/`, UTF-8, LF; magic line
  `%dyne 0.1`, MAJOR.MINOR versioning
- three sections: headers, `--- log ---`, `--- body ---`
- closed header set v1: `Title`, `Source`, `Target`, `Created`,
  `Author` required; `Closes` and `Ref` optional, repeatable, values
  opaque non-empty lines that dyne never resolves (the composition
  seam); no Status header ever -- state is the DAG
- log entry grammar: `TIMESTAMP author TYPE ...`, one line per entry;
  types `opened`, `note`, `verdict APPROVED|REROLL|ESCALATE sha=`,
  `ci pass|fail sha=`, comment anchors `path:line@sha`
- body = the discussion: opening post is the author's description,
  later comments are timestamp-attributed prose blocks, append-only by
  convention
- document the merge regime: `merge=union` on `tickets/merges/*.dyne` via
  .gitattributes (deployed by `dyne init`, 0274), entries reordered by
  timestamp at display time, duplicate headers a hard `check` error

## Historical exit criteria

These criteria are candidates only. Before work starts, revise them to match
the decision in 0271; if Dyne is not justified, do not implement them.

- [ ] spec document merged (embedded serving via `dyne spec` lands with
      0273/0274)
- [ ] every constraint above is a testable statement, in the spec's
      validate-rules style

## Design reassessment (2026-11-04)

Git notes are the review-evidence store, as the author confirmed. The earlier
`tickets/reviews/` proposal is superseded. Read `docs/dyne-review-contract.md`
for the current harness evidence and the remaining decision. The scope above
records the original design candidates; it does not authorize implementation.
Ticket 0271 must first establish a concrete unmet need and decide whether a
separate Dyne object is warranted. Subsequent format and implementation work
is conditional on that decision. This ticket remains open.
